    "title": "RE Foundations / 12A / The Robots Are Coming!",
    "text_type": "informational",
    "audience": {
      "grade_band": "upper_elementary"
    },
    "language": "en"
  },
  "content": {
    "paragraphs": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "order": 1,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s1",
            "text": "You have probably seen robots in movies such as Star Wars or Transformers."
          },
          {
            "id": "s2",
            "text": "But soon, robots may be part of our daily lives."
          },
          {
            "id": "s3",
            "text": "Today’s scientists are working on robots with various skills."
          },
          {
            "id": "s4",
            "text": "For example, it is likely that robots will soon help take care of children or the elderly, 1 or do dangerous jobs such as fighting fires."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "order": 2,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s5",
            "text": "Early robots were made to do simple things, mainly in factories."
          },
          {
            "id": "s6",
            "text": "Since then, robots have changed a lot."
          },
          {
            "id": "s7",
            "text": "Humans operated these early robots."
          },
          {
            "id": "s8",
            "text": "Today’s robots - like Honda’s ASIMO - work on their own."
          },
          {
            "id": "s9",
            "text": "ASIMO can run, climb stairs, and dance."
          },
          {
            "id": "s10",
            "text": "Boston Dynamics’ Atlas robot can run fast, jump, and even do backflips 2 - all on two legs!"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "order": 3,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s11",
            "text": "Then there are robots designed to be like humans."
          },
          {
            "id": "s12",
            "text": "These robots have faces and can also talk."
          },
          {
            "id": "s13",
            "text": "Such robots can learn new things, and show us how they “feel.”"
          },
          {
            "id": "s14",
            "text": "Sophia—a social robot—has a face that looks so human she sometimes makes people feel uncomfortable. 1"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "order": 4,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s15",
            "text": "Scientists aren’t just building humanlike robots."
          },
          {
            "id": "s16",
            "text": "They are also making robots that look and act like animals."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "order": 5,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s17",
            "text": "At NASA, for example, scientists have made a robot snake."
          },
          {
            "id": "s18",
            "text": "These snake-bots can enter holes and move over rough ground."
          },
          {
            "id": "s19",
            "text": "They might one day help scientists look for signs of life on Mars."
          },
          {
            "id": "s20",
            "text": "Other animal robots include the frog-bot, which can jump over objects, and the sticky-bot, which can walk up walls."
          },
          {
            "id": "s21",
            "text": "There are also doglike robots, like SpotMini, which have four legs and can run at high speed."
          },
          {
            "id": "s22",
            "text": "Who knows?"
          },
          {
            "id": "s23",
            "text": "Perhaps in the future, we’ll all have our own robot pet."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
